/** The answer to POST /api/v1/messages, the same shape for a first send and for an identical retry. `duplicate` says the server had it already. It carries what JARVIS stores in one transaction with the accepted message: its receipts (none yet) and the sender's own item after it, at the server's revision, so no local copy of `on_message` can diverge. */
